// Override of the packaged Packages/Default/Side Bar Mount Point.sublime-menu.
// Sublime merges this file's entries into whichever side bar section carries
// the matching id -- "folder_commands" in Default/Side Bar.sublime-menu -- and
// only for top-level project folders. That scoping is the reason to add
// "Remove Other Folders from Project" here rather than to the main menu: a
// sub-folder has nothing to remove, and this file is how Sublime expresses
// "top-level folders only". See README.md "Remove Folder from Project".
//
// The shipped copy is the first two entries verbatim, so ordering inside the
// section is ours: Remove Folder from Project first, its bulk counterpart
// directly below, matching Close Tab / Close Other Tabs in the tab menu.
//
// This file freezes the menu at build 4200. After a Sublime update, re-sync
// against the shipped copy:
//   unzip -p "<install>/Packages/Default.sublime-package" "Side Bar Mount Point.sublime-menu"
//   # <install> = /opt/sublime_text on Linux
//   #             /Applications/Sublime Text.app/Contents/MacOS on macOS
[
	{ "caption": "-", "id": "folder_commands" },
	{ "caption": "Remove Folder from Project", "command": "remove_folder", "args": { "dirs": []} },
	{ "caption": "Remove Other Folders from Project", "command": "remove_other_folders_from_project", "args": { "dirs": []} }
]
